  🔴 Critical / Logic Errors

  1. server.ts:42 — VERSION hardcoded, permanently stale
  const VERSION = '1.2.0' — server still reports 1.2.0 to every MCP client even though the package is 1.2.2. The server and CLI have
   separate VERSION constants that drift independently. Fix: read from package.json once at startup.

  2. server.ts:729 — phase: 8 in veto_status response
  veto_status tells every AI client "I am Phase 8" with capabilities from Phase 8 only. The tool list is missing all 19 tools added
  in Phases 13–15 (watch, workflow, explain, plugins, docs_fetch, context_status, task_parse, usage_status, audit_log, health,
  ci_gate, etc.). Any AI client using veto_status to decide what tools are available gets a completely wrong answer.

  3. veto_task_parse — produces fake structured output
  - Complexity is Math.round((i / steps.length) * 10) + 3 — index position, not real complexity
  - suggested_agent is always 'coder' — the router is never consulted
  - estimated_hours is always 2 — never estimated
  - depends_on is always [task-${i}] — always a linear chain, real dependencies never inferred
  - The "task DAG" it produces is completely fabricated around step order

  4. getHealthStats() — latency metric is wrong
  avg_council_latency_ms measures the gap between consecutive debates (time from one debate to the next), not the duration of a
  debate. A user who runs two debates 10 minutes apart will see avg_council_latency_ms: 600000. It's measuring idle time, not
  performance.

  5. veto_ci_gate and veto_diff_review — different verdict logic for the same job
  - veto_diff_review uses critical_count / high_count from analysis
  - veto_ci_gate uses raw confidence floats with magic thresholds (0.4, 0.5, 0.6, 0.7)
  - Same 3-scan parallel pattern duplicated in full across both handlers

