  6. searchKnowledge() — SQL string interpolation
  db.exec(\UPDATE knowledge_base SET accessed_count = accessed_count + 1 WHERE id IN (${ids})`)` — UUIDs make exploitation unlikely
  but the pattern is wrong. Should use a prepared statement loop or a parameterised batch.

  7. getAuditLog() — agent filter silently ignored for council events
  for (const r of councilRows) {
    if (opts.agent) continue; // ← drops ALL council rows if agent filter is set, no warning
  If you call veto_audit_log with { agent: "security-scanner" } you get zero council events with no explanation. Should either
  include them or return a note.

  8. council/index.ts — Promise.resolve() wrapping sync functions
  All 7 council agents are synchronous but wrapped in Promise.resolve(). This is unnecessary overhead and misleads readers into
  thinking the agents are async. They should be called directly and results passed to Promise.all only if they ever become genuinely
   async.

  9. executor.ts:141 — plan confidence hardcoded at 0.8
  Every plan() call returns confidence: 0.8 regardless of content. The CI gate and workflow pipeline use this confidence to make
  pass/fail decisions — they're making verdicts based on a constant.

  10. veto_diff_review + veto_ci_gate — child_process dynamic import in hot path
  Both handlers do await import('node:child_process') inside the request handler every time they're called. This should be a
  top-level import.

  11. local.ts — closeSession() is dead code
  closeSession() is exported but never called anywhere in server.ts. Sessions are never closed, only saved.

  12. docs_cache User-Agent hardcoded wrong version
  headers: { 'User-Agent': 'veto-mcp/1.1.0' } in fetchAndCacheDocs for crates.io — stale version string baked in.

