  Phase 16 — Real Intelligence (v1.3.0)

  #25 — LLM-backed agents (the #1 missing feature)
  Every agent currently returns heuristic output. The plan() and analyze() functions return hardcoded templates. Agents should
  optionally call an LLM (via the user's existing subscription — Claude/Gemini/Codex) to generate real, context-aware responses.
  This is what Context7 (53k stars) and claude-task-master (26k stars) built their following on. Without this, Veto's agents are
  sophisticated pattern matchers, not real advisors.

  #26 — Auto session save
  When token_count passes 70% in any session, automatically call saveSession() in the background. Zero user action required. This is
   the most-requested quality-of-life feature for persistent memory tools.

  #27 — GitHub PR integration
  veto_pr_review — pass a GitHub PR URL, Veto fetches the diff via GitHub API and runs the full veto_ci_gate pipeline. Outputs
  structured review comments ready to post. This collapses the most common workflow (review PR → fix issues) into one tool call.

